237 L 1286 4237 Q 1210 4237 1210 4166 L 1094 2778 Q 1088 2733 1113 2710 Q 1139 2688 1171 2701 Q 1408 2822 1648 2915 Q 1888 3008 2234 3008 Q 2656 3008 3021 2854 Q 3386 2701 3606 2381 Q 3827 2061 3827 1555 Q 3827 1043 3593 681 Q 3360 320 2947 128 Q 2534 -64 2003 -64 Q 1517 -64 1085 105 Q 653 275 352 602 Q 326 640 323 669 Q 320 698 365 730 L 640 954 Q 691 992 749 934 Q 922 774 1088 652 Q 1254 531 1456 464 Q 1658 397 1926 397 Q 2342 397 2630 544 Q 2918 691 3072 950 Q 3226 1210 3226 1536 Q 3226 1882 3078 2102 Q 2931 2323 2684 2432 Q 2438 2541 2138 2541 Q 1798 2541 1529 2419 Q 1261 2298 1037 2163 Q 986 2138 973 2144 Q 960 2150 922 2170 L 608 2349 Q 550 2381 553 2397 Q 557 2413 563 2490 L 736 4659 Q 742 4717 764 4733 Q 787 4749 877 4749 L 3482 4749 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(68.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-89\" transform=\"translate(89.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-85\" transform=\"translate(155.5 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_12\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(166.013975 72.452211) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(68.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-85\" transform=\"translate(89.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(155.109375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_13\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(249.6714 117.193263) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" d=\"M 2637 486 Q 2707 486 2707 422 L 2707 64 Q 2707 45 2691 22 Q 2675 0 2637 0 L 390 0 Q 320 0 320 64 L 320 422 Q 320 486 390 486 L 1197 486 Q 1248 486 1248 518 L 1248 4038 Q 1248 4102 1190 4090 L 397 3795 Q 314 3776 314 3872 L 314 4128 Q 314 4173 326 4189 Q 339 4205 378 4224 L 1325 4698 Q 1389 4730 1427 4739 Q 1466 4749 1517 4749 L 1792 4749 Q 1862 4749 1862 4672 L 1862 531 Q 1862 486 1901 486 L 2637 486 L 2637 486 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(68.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(89.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-85\" transform=\"translate(136.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_14\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(332.301325 123.584842) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(68.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(89.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(136.203125 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pbe2d6d2ed7\"><rect x=\"43.373\" y=\"10.824\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 2 · Increase in store costs this year ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Wages ($0.95M) and energy ($0.50M) explain 85% of the increase. The wage rise is driven by the legal minimum wage, so it won't reverse.</p> <p>To earn $5.4M again at today's $9 per basket and $15.2M of store costs, Meadowlane needs ($5.4M + $15.2M) ÷ $9 = <b>2.29M baskets</b>, 15% more than today and more than it ever had.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> volume alone won't fix this. Meadowlane needs to win back some baskets <i>and</i> run its stores more efficiently.</p>"},{"q":"What would you recommend to the owners?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p><b>Win back shoppers near the discounter</b></p><ul><li>Price-match 100 everyday staples; keep margin on fresh, local and deli</li> <li>A loyalty scheme so Meadowlane knows who has stopped coming</li></ul> <p><b>Lower store costs</b></p><ul><li>Self-checkouts and staff rotas matched to footfall by hour</li> <li>Energy: LED lighting and doors on fridges (often a 1 to 2 year payback)</li></ul> <p><b>Find out first:</b> is the basket loss all at the store near the discounter? If so, it's a local problem, not a brand problem.</p>"}],"reco":"Profit halved because store costs rose $1.7M (mostly wages and energy) and Meadowlane lost 5% of its baskets after a discounter opened; supplier inflation was passed on in full, so it isn't the cause. Volume alone can't fix it: getting back to $5.4M would need 15% more baskets. I recommend price-matching everyday staples at the affected store, plus self-checkouts, footfall-based rotas and an energy programme. Risk: price-matching erodes margin if it spreads beyond staples. Next step: check basket trends store by store.","great":["Builds a bridge instead of listing causes","Notices price and cost of goods cancel out","Turns 'win back volume' into a number and sees it isn't enough","Asks whether the loss is local to one store"],"id":23,"slug":"meadowlane-grocers"}